.TH CHANGELOG-LINT 8 "July 2026" "changelog 1.0.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
changelog lint \- validate fragment files for correctness and consistency
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B changelog lint
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfragment\-files...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBlint\fR command validates one or more fragment files (or all fragments in a directory)
for structural correctness, required fields, and best practices. It checks for common
issues like missing dates, invalid categories, malformed YAML, and content problems.

Linting is essential before releasing to ensure changelog quality and consistency. The tool
provides both basic validation and strict mode with additional checks.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.

.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dir\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Main fragment directory to validate. Defaults to \fIchangelogs/fragments/\fR in the current project root.
.PP
Can be combined with positional arguments for mixed validation (specific files + directory).

.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-strict\fR
Enable strict validation mode with additional checks:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Require date field on all fragments
.IP \(bu 2
Validate link syntax in fragment content
.IP \(bu 2
Check for empty body text
.IP \(bu 2
Detect colon-in-string issues that cause PyYAML parsing problems
.RE

.TP
\fB\-\-page\-size\fR=\fIN\fR
Number of entries per page when displaying results interactively. Defaults to 10.
.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.PP
Specific fragment file paths to validate individually. If omitted, all fragments in the
specified directory (or \fB\-\-dir\fR) are validated.

Valid extensions: .yml, .yaml, .md
.SH VALIDATION RULES
.TP
.B Basic checks (always enabled):
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
File exists and is readable
.IP \(bu 2
YAML syntax is valid
.IP \(bu 2
Required fields present: category, issue, text/title
.IP \(bu 2
Category matches known values (bugfixes, minor_changes, etc.)
.IP \(bu 2
Issue ID format is reasonable (non-empty, alphanumeric with hyphens)
.RE

.TP
.B Strict checks (\fB\-\-strict\fR flag required):
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Date field present and in YYYY-MM-DD format
.IP \(bu 2
No colon-in-string issues that break YAML parsing
.IP \(bu 2
Body text is not empty or whitespace-only
.IP \(bu 2
Link syntax (if any) follows valid URL patterns
.RE

.TP
.B Common issues detected:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fIColon in unquoted strings\fR \- "Fixed issue: crash" parses as dict instead of string
.IP \(bu 2
\fIMissing required fields\fR \- Fragments without category or issue ID
.IP \(bu 2
\fIInvalid categories\fR \- Typos like "bugfix" instead of "bugfixes"
.IP \(bu 2
\fIDuplicate fragment names\fR - Same filename in same directory (collision detection)
.RE
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
\fB0\fR
All fragments passed validation successfully.

.TP
\fB1\fR
One or more validation errors found. Output lists each error with file and line reference.

.TP
\fB2\fR
Internal error (directory not found, permission denied, etc.).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Validate all fragments in default directory:
.nf
    changelog lint
.fi

.TP
Validate specific fragment files:
.nf
    changelog lint changelogs/fragments/PG-001-bugfixes.yml changelogs/fragments/IMP-456-enhancement.yml
.fi

.TP
Run strict validation with additional checks:
.nf
    changelog lint --strict
.fi

.TP
Validate fragments in a custom directory:
.nf
    changelog lint -d /path/to/custom/fragments/
.fi

.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
.PP
Validation results display one line per error:
.IP \(bu 2
\fI<filename>: <error description>\fR
.PP
After listing all errors, a summary shows total count. Use \fB\-\-strict\fR for comprehensive validation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.TP
\fBchangelog-add(8)\fR \- Create new fragment files (with linting recommendations)
.TP
\fBchangelog-release(8)\fR \- Generate release notes from validated fragments
